/* Layout for the new-character SKILLS tab (Tier 4 #4 slice 3).
   Linked AFTER newchar_common.rcss, so a same-specificity rule here wins — which is how the
   meter pips below re-tune the shared pip sizing.

   The meta bar, the dotted rules, the columns, the row, the cursor cell, the cost cell, the
   name cell, the detail panel and the hint are all the SHARED row-list vocabulary in
   newchar_common.rcss. What is local to this step is the part of a row that carries a
   MAGNITUDE — the steppers, the meter and the level cell — plus the aptitude matrix.
   See plans/charcreation-skills-matrix.md. */

body {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
}

.nc-panel {
    width: 98%;
    height: 98%;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
}

.nc-steps {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
}

.nc-step {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
}

/* ── COLUMN HEADING SIGIL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The same glyph the radar sector and the detail panel's art slot draw, so a column, its
   sector and its description cannot disagree about which category is being read. */
.nc-col-sigil {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 14dp;
    height: 14dp;
    margin-right: 6dp;
}

/* ── ROW MAGNITUDE CELLS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Steppers flank the meter, minus on its left and plus on its right, so the mouse gesture
   is spatially the same as the LEFT/RIGHT keys. */
.nc-cell-step {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 14dp;
    text-align: center;
    color: {{fg4}};
}

.nc-cell-step:hover {
    color: {{yellow}};
}

/* At the floor or the cap. Still drawn, so the row does not change shape — but this is a
   click target for something that SPENDS points, so it must not offer a hover affordance
   when pressing it will do nothing. Same pattern the stats steppers use. */
.nc-cell-step.off {
    color: {{bg3}};
}

.nc-cell-step.off:hover {
    color: {{bg3}};
}

.nc-cell-meter {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 84dp;
    height: 12dp;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    margin: 0 4dp;
}

/* The shared pip sizing is tuned for the STATS card's taller meter, and this sheet is linked
   after the shared one — so the HEIGHT channel has to be restated here or it is lost. It is
   load-bearing: filled pips are TALLER as well as brighter, which is what keeps the meter
   readable in greyscale and for any form of colour blindness. Colour is the second channel
   here, never the only one. */
.nc-cell-meter .nc-pip {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    height: 5dp;
    margin-right: 2dp;
}

.nc-cell-meter .nc-pip.on {
    height: 11dp;
}

/* A level the profession grants after creation: present, but plainly not something the player
   bought. Three classes, so it beats the shared filled-pip colour on specificity alone. */
.nc-cell-meter .nc-pip.bonus {
    background-color: {{blue}};
}

/* The number the meter draws, plus what the profession adds — because colour alone must not
   be the only carrier of a quantity. Right-aligned so the levels stack into a gutter. */
.nc-cell-lvl {
    display: block;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 40dp;
    text-align: right;
    margin-right: 8dp;
}

/* ── APTITUDE MATRIX ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   A dot radar beside the lists: one filled sector per display category, its depth that
   category's share of the strongest one, with a beam sweeping round it.

   The disc is a FIXED square, not a flexible box: a circle cannot be derived from a height
   the layout chooses, and both sides must agree. 13 rows of 13 cells at 14dp is 182dp, and
   the cell count is nc_apt::grid in src/newchar_aptitude.h — the one coupling between this
   sheet and that header.

   It cannot simply grow to fill the column either: the legend under it needs one row per
   category, and a taller disc pushes those rows out of the stage. What made the wedges
   comparable was scaling them against the strongest category rather than against every skill
   at MAX_SKILL — see sync_apt. */
.nc-apt-wrap {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 196dp;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
}

.nc-apt {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 182dp;
    height: 182dp;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    margin: 6dp 0;
}

.nc-apt-row {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
}

/* Every dot's colour AND alpha is written per frame by C++; dots outside the disc are fully
   transparent, which is what makes a square grid read as a circle. Nothing here encodes the
   shape, so the geometry stays testable without a document. */
.nc-apt-dot {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    height: 8dp;
    margin: 0 3dp;
    border-radius: 4dp;
    background-color: transparent;
}

/* Legend beneath the disc. An unlabelled radar is decoration, so each sector gets its sigil,
   its name and the count it is drawn from.

   `overflow: hidden` because this box can be shrunk below its content: it is the flexible
   element under a fixed-size disc, and a mod adding display categories adds rows. Clipped is
   recoverable; drawing over the rule and the detail panel below is not. */
.nc-apt-legend {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    overflow: hidden;
}

.nc-apt-leg {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    height: 16dp;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
}

.nc-apt-leg-icon {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 12dp;
    height: 12dp;
    margin-right: 6dp;
}

.nc-apt-leg-name {
    display: block;
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    white-space: nowrap;
    overflow: hidden;
}

.nc-apt-leg-val {
    display: block;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
}

/* ── DETAIL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Same as the traits step: this tab spends its height on the lists, so the shared panel gets
   the shorter of the two heights. */
.nc-info-panel {
    height: 196dp;
}
